' A real, ordinary ArcoBASIC program meant to be compiled BY the Fission
' Compiler Substrate's native x86-64 backend (fission/amir/lower_x86_64.abas)
' -- see fission/tests/native_programs/hello_native.abas's own header
' comment for the directory convention. Exercises the real HOST-FUNCTION
' BRIDGE (fission/amir/lower_x86_64.abas's own Fission_X86_64HostFunctionTable):
' genuinely compiled native machine code (fission/native_runtime/
' host_bridge.c, compiled once by the system's own C compiler as a
' development-time build step -- see that file's own header comment),
' linked directly into this program's own final ELF64 by The Arcology
' Fusion Linker via a real ELF64 object-file reader
' (fission/amir/elf_object.abas), NOT a bytecode-VM host-call dispatch and
' NOT a from-scratch ArcoBASIC reimplementation. All 7 real String.*
' functions this first slice supports: Length, Contains, IndexOf,
' StartsWith, EndsWith (all confirmed against the oracle first), Trim and
' Slice (both real, mmap-allocated new strings, proving the host bridge's
' own memory allocation path -- a raw mmap syscall, no libc -- works
' correctly and the returned pointer is a genuinely valid, NUL-terminated
' string this backend's own machinery can consume right back).
'
' Expected output verified against legacy `ArcoFission compile-run` on this
' identical source as the equivalence-testing oracle.
PRINT String.Length("Hello World")
PRINT String.Length("")
PRINT String.Contains("Hello World", "World")
PRINT String.Contains("Hello World", "xyz")
PRINT String.IndexOf("Hello World", "World")
PRINT String.IndexOf("Hello World", "xyz")
PRINT String.StartsWith("Hello World", "Hello")
PRINT String.StartsWith("Hello World", "World")
PRINT String.EndsWith("Hello World", "World")
PRINT String.Trim("  hi  ")
PRINT String.Slice("Hello World", 6, 5)
PRINT String.Slice("Hello World", 0, 5)

' A host function's own result flows correctly back through this
' backend's own EVERYTHING ELSE -- stored into a variable, concatenated,
' passed to another host function, used as a branch condition.
trimmed = String.Trim("  padded  ")
PRINT trimmed + "!"
IF String.Contains(trimmed, "padded") THEN
    PRINT "yes"
END IF
PRINT String.Length(trimmed)
